[statement]
apk reads the names a request states after the repositories', unlike the
world's (`installed/the-world-s-names-are-read-before-the-installed-database-s`):
a request changes no name's place in its table. `au` and `xp` share a
bucket, and `xp`, listed later, is read last and walked first. Were the
request's `xp` read before the repositories, `au` would be read last and
walked first.

[repository]
P:base
V:1

P:au
V:1
i:base

P:xp
V:1
i:base

[request]
base
xp

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install base 1
install xp 1
install au 1
